{
  // Build-time compiler options.
  //
  // WHY A SEPARATE CONFIG EXISTS
  //
  // `npm run build` runs `tsc`, and `tsc` compiles every file under `src` - including the 34
  // test files. That put the entire test suite into `dist/`, which means the production image
  // shipped test code, and a test file could in principle be imported by something in the
  // runtime graph.
  //
  // Excluding tests from `tsconfig.json` itself would be the wrong fix: that config is also
  // what `npm run typecheck` uses, and typechecking the tests is most of the value. Losing
  // that to save 400 kB in an image would be a bad trade.
  //
  // So this extends the main config and narrows only the file set. Everything else - strict
  // flags, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`, the lot - is inherited unchanged, which means the
  // build cannot silently compile under different rules than the typecheck.
  //
  // `e2e/` is excluded too: Playwright specs run from source under its own runner and must not
  // be emitted into the image at all. They stay in `tsconfig.json`, so `npm run typecheck`
  // still covers them, which is the point of the two-config split.
  //
  // Deliberately narrow otherwise: only `*.test.ts` is excluded. Fuzzers, benchmarks and helper files
  // that live outside the test naming convention stay in, because they are not what bloats the
  // image and removing them by pattern is how a real file goes missing.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist", "src/**/*.test.ts", "e2e"]
}
